2. In these Rules —
“eligible parking place” has the meaning given by rule 4;
“private dwelling-house” means any building, flat or tenement wholly or principally used or occupied for residential purposes;
“registered owner”, in relation to a heavy vehicle, means the person who is registered under the Road Traffic Act 1961 as the owner of the heavy vehicle.

6. The requirements for parking a heavy vehicle at an eligible parking place are as follows:
(a)a lodgement has been made to the Authority in accordance with rule 7 for the parking of the heavy vehicle at the eligible parking place by the registered owner of the heavy vehicle;
(b)the heavy vehicle is parked at the eligible parking place during the period specified in the lodgement;
(c)the registered owner has received a notice from the Authority acknowledging the person’s lodgement under rule 7(3);
(d)the lodgement has not lapsed under rule 8;
(e)the registered owner has the consent of the owner or occupier of the eligible parking place to park the vehicle at that eligible parking place.

7.—(1) The registered owner of a heavy vehicle, or a person who has purchased or intends to purchase a heavy vehicle (each called Y), may make a lodgement for the purposes of rule 5 through the Authority’s Internet website at https://www.onemotoring.lta.gov.sg.
(2) A lodgement, in relation to a heavy vehicle, must be accompanied by the following information and documents:
(a)Y’s name;
(b)the vehicle registration number of the heavy vehicle (including the index mark and suffix) or the chassis number of the heavy vehicle;
(c)the address of the eligible parking place;
(d)the name of the owner or occupier of the eligible parking place and that owner’s or occupier’s business address;
(e)the period the heavy vehicle is to be parked at the eligible parking place (which must not exceed 2 years);
(f)except where Y is also the owner or occupier of the eligible parking place — evidence that the consent or permission of the owner or occupier of the eligible parking place has been obtained to allow the parking of the heavy vehicle at the eligible parking place;
(g)any other information or documents specified by the Authority.
(3) Upon receipt of a lodgement in relation to a heavy vehicle in accordance with paragraphs (1) and (2), the Authority must issue a notice acknowledging the receipt of the lodgement to the person who made the lodgement under paragraph (1).

8. A lodgement made under rule 7(1) to park a heavy vehicle at an eligible parking place is treated to have lapsed if —
(a)the eligible parking place specified in the lodgement is no longer an eligible parking place;
(b)the registered owner of the heavy vehicle no longer has the consent or permission of the owner or occupier of the eligible parking place to park the heavy vehicle at that eligible parking place;
(c)the registration of the heavy vehicle is cancelled under section 27(1) of the Road Traffic Act 1961; or
(d)any information or document submitted in relation to the lodgement is false or misleading.
